{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788350813,"nonce":"hcsvN9n8mBEUkKDrZ9QnEzldS58=","title":"Run `m1-20260901`, mechanism **F2** in the postmortem, which cost **Marco**:","message":"```\ndesignate {type:\"hunt\", ...}  -\u003e  accepted: 6\n```\n\n...and nothing ever happened, because every target was outside the colony's `Area_Allowed`. The envelope was truthful and useless: six designations were genuinely created. No pawn could ever act on one.\n\nThis is already a playbook lesson ([[a-designation-outside-the-allowed-area-does-nothing]], indexed Critical) and it belongs in the mod. The test is one the codebase already runs elsewhere: `posture` uses `InAllowedArea` for its `area_bound` reading, so the routine, the safety of calling it, and its semantics are all established.\n\n\n1. `designate` runs `InAllowedArea` per target and reports per-target reachability. Applies to every designation type that produces work for a pawn, `hunt` and `mine` first.\n2. `accepted` is no longer a single number covering both cases. The envelope distinguishes accepted-and-actionable from accepted-but-unreachable, and names the area that excludes the target. Whether an all-unreachable batch is a refusal or a loud report is the worker's call to make and record: the material-shortfall precedent in `place-layout` argues for refusing a batch where **no** target is actionable, while a mixed batch reports.\n3. Reachability is reported as the game computes it, not re-derived. Cite the member you call, per the standing \"the gate lives in the widget\" rule.\n4. `checklists/turn.md` §materials-designation-loop cites the new field, and the existing playbook lesson is amended to name it.\n5. `accept/\u003cid\u003e-designate-reach.py` on a bench: `designate hunt` a target outside every allowed area, assert the refusal or the report says so; a target inside, assert it is clean; a mixed batch, assert both rows are distinguishable.\n\n\nC2 of `next-run.md` is the largest single cause of the wipe: **128 designated `MineableSteel` cells, never mined.** Area exclusion is not the whole of C2 — work priorities are the rest — but it is the half the mod can decide, and it shares a file and a checklist section with `855117a`.\n\n\nThis is item 4 of the repair round's bench list: *`designate hunt` a target outside every allowed area — the refusal or the report says so, rather than `accepted: N` and silence.*","files":null}]}